Seeded defect for tools/aot-smoke/run.sh (the call-site check of Consumer.Linq)

Hand-made: DocumentCollection.CreateIndexAsync and its IDocumentCollection declaration lose
their [RequiresDynamicCode] (both, or the build fails with IL3051), and the analyzer is silenced
around the inner call to CollectionIndexManager.CreateIndex with #pragma warning disable IL3050,
the way BLite.Core keeps its build green elsewhere. BLite.Core and BLite still build with
TreatWarningsAsErrors; the method still compiles its key selector at runtime.

With it applied, the call of CreateIndexAsync in Consumer.Linq/LinqCalls.cs:22 loses its IL3050,
which AOT_LIMITATIONS.md promises at the call site, and the warning moves into BLite.Core, where
the Consumer.Linq "additional" count reports it as not registered (osx-arm64, 2026-10-17):
    FAIL    call site LinqCalls.cs:22 CreateIndexAsync: expected IL3050, absent
    new: src/BLite.Core/Collections/DocumentCollection.cs(1025): AOT analysis warning IL3050:
         BLite.Core.Collections.DocumentCollection`2.<CreateIndexAsync>d__60`1.MoveNext(): Using member
         'BLite.Core.Indexing.CollectionIndexManager`2<TId,T>.CreateIndex<TKey>(...)' ...
    FAIL    Consumer.Linq additional: 12 BLite warnings, expected 0; 1 not registered; known: A6 x10, A7 x1

Reproduce: tools/aot-smoke/run.sh --prove-seeds create-index-unannotated
   or:    git apply --ignore-whitespace tools/aot-smoke/seeds/aot-smoke.create-index-unannotated.patch && tools/aot-smoke/run.sh
Restore:   git checkout -- src

The source files mix LF and CRLF line endings; apply with --ignore-whitespace if the patch was
normalised. Never commit the seeded state.

